The validation is split across two places: an early return for `0 | Infinity`, then a ternary for positive integers with an implicit fallback to 27. This makes the overall logic harder to follow at a glance. Consider consolidating into a single expression, e.g.:
```typescript
const effectiveLimit =
  maxPresetColors > 0 && Number.isFinite(maxPresetColors)
    ? Math.floor(maxPresetColors)
    : maxPresetColors === 0 || maxPresetColors === Infinity
    ? Infinity
    : 27;
return effectiveLimit === Infinity ? combined : combined.slice(-effectiveLimit);
```
